IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: ss 375 and 376 -- what a foreign company must state about itself on its documents
-- and in its premises, and how a document is served on it. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind);
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Section 375: the name, the place of formation, the notice of limited liability, the unique entity number`

DECLARE `s 375 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 375(1)(b) cause its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated to be stated in legible romanised letters`
    `s 375(1)(c) cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given`
    `s 375(3) cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form`

-- src:24552 | Obligation to state name of foreign company, whether limited,
-- src:24553 | and country where incorporated
-- src:24555 | 375.—(1) A foreign company must —
-- src:24557 | (a) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:24559 | (b) cause its name and the place where it is formed or
-- src:24560 | incorporated to be stated in legible romanised letters on all
-- src:24561 | its bill‑heads and letter paper and in all its notices,
-- src:24562 | prospectuses and other official publications; and
@ref s 375(1)(b) (src:24552-24562)
GIVEN `the document is one of its bill-heads, letter paper, notices, prospectuses or other official publications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated are stated on the document in legible romanised letters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(1)(b) the document states the name and the place of formation in legible romanised letters` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is one of its bill-heads, letter paper, notices, prospectuses or other official publications`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on all its bill-heads and letter paper and in all its notices, prospectuses and other official publications" names the documents it reaches; a document outside that description is not covered
    ELSE (IF `its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated are stated on the document in legible romanised letters`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A foreign company must — ... (b) cause its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated to be stated in legible romanised letters on all its bill-heads and letter paper and in all its notices, prospectuses and other official publications" (a duty not met)

@ref s 375(1)(b) (src:24555-24562)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 375 act`
`s 375(1)(b) the foreign company must cause its name and place of formation to be stated in legible romanised letters` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 375(1)(b) cause its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated to be stated in legible romanised letters`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 375(1)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the name and place of formation were not stated in legible romanised letters" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (c) "if the liability of its members is limited (unless the last word of its name is the word "Limited" or "Berhad" or the abbreviation "Ltd." or "Bhd."), cause notice of that fact".
-- src:24564 | (c) if the liability of its members is limited (unless the last
-- src:24565 | word of its name is the word “Limited” or “Berhad” or the
-- src:24566 | abbreviation “Ltd.” or “Bhd.”), cause notice of that fact —
-- src:24568 | (i) to be stated in legible characters in every prospectus
-- src:24569 | issued by it and in all its bill‑heads, letter paper,
-- src:24570 | notices, and other official publications in Singapore;
-- src:24571 | and
-- src:24573 | (ii) except in the case of a banking corporation, to be
-- src:24574 | exhibited outside its registered office and every place
-- src:24575 | of business established by it in Singapore.
@ref s 375(1)(c) (src:24564-24575)
GIVEN `the liability of its members is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last word of the foreign company's name` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` MEANS
    IF NOT `the liability of its members is limited`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the liability of its members is limited" (a duty gated by "if": fork F-D1)
    ELSE (IF `the last word of the foreign company's name` EQUALS "Limited" OR `the last word of the foreign company's name` EQUALS "Berhad" OR `the last word of the foreign company's name` EQUALS "Ltd." OR `the last word of the foreign company's name` EQUALS "Bhd."
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the last word of its name is the word “Limited” or “Berhad” or the abbreviation “Ltd.” or “Bhd.”"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 375(1)(c)(i) (src:24568-24571)
GIVEN `the document is a prospectus issued by the foreign company, or one of its bill-heads, letter paper, notices or other official publications in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice that the liability of its members is limited is stated on the document in legible characters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(1)(c)(i) the document states notice that the liability of the members is limited in legible characters` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is a prospectus issued by the foreign company, or one of its bill-heads, letter paper, notices or other official publications in Singapore`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in every prospectus issued by it and in all its bill-heads, letter paper, notices, and other official publications in Singapore" names the documents it reaches
    ELSE (IF `the notice that the liability of its members is limited is stated on the document in legible characters`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cause notice of that fact — (i) to be stated in legible characters in every prospectus issued by it ..." (a duty not met)

@ref s 375(1)(c)(ii) (src:24573-24575)
GIVEN `the foreign company is a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(1)(c)(ii) the foreign company must exhibit the notice outside its registered office and every place of business it has established in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "banking corporation" the body is a banking corporation` `the foreign company is a banking corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) except in the case of a banking corporation, to be exhibited outside its registered office and every place of business established by it in Singapore"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 375(1)(c) (src:24564-24575)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 375 act`
`s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 375(1)(c) cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 375(1)(c) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "notice that the liability of its members is limited was not given" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (2) "deemed not to have been complied with unless the name of the company is stated on such document in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters".
-- src:24579 | (2) Where the name of a foreign company is indicated on any of the
-- src:24580 | documents referred to in subsection (1) in characters or in any other
-- src:24581 | way than by the use of romanised letters, this section relating to the
-- src:24582 | statement of its name is deemed not to have been complied with
-- src:24583 | unless the name of the company is stated on such document in
-- src:24588 | romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters so exhibited
-- src:24589 | or stated on the relevant document.
@ref s 375(2) (src:24579-24589)
GIVEN `the name is indicated on the document in characters, or in any other way than by the use of romanised letters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is stated on the document in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters so exhibited or stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(2) the section relating to the statement of the name is deemed not to have been complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT `the name is indicated on the document in characters, or in any other way than by the use of romanised letters`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the name of a foreign company is indicated on any of the documents referred to in subsection (1) in characters or in any other way than by the use of romanised letters" names the case it speaks to
    ELSE (IF `the name is stated on the document in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters so exhibited or stated`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deemed not to have been complied with unless the name of the company is stated on such document in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters": once they are, the subsection does not say the section is complied with
          ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- the deeming applies: "this section relating to the statement of its name is deemed not to have been complied with unless ..."

-- (3) the unique entity number, issued by the Registrar, must appear in a legible form on all business letters, statements of account, invoices, official notices and publications.
-- src:24593 | (3) The unique entity number of a foreign company, issued by the
-- src:24594 | Registrar, must appear in a legible form on all business letters,
-- src:24595 | statements of account, invoices, official notices and publications of or
-- src:24596 | purporting to be issued or signed by or on behalf of the company.
@ref s 375(3) (src:24593-24596)
GIVEN `the document is a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication of or purporting to be issued or signed by or on behalf of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unique entity number issued by the Registrar appears on the document in a legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(3) the document shows the unique entity number in a legible form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication of or purporting to be issued or signed by or on behalf of the foreign company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on all business letters, statements of account, invoices, official notices and publications of or purporting to be issued or signed by or on behalf of the company" names the documents it reaches
    ELSE (IF `the unique entity number issued by the Registrar appears on the document in a legible form`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The unique entity number of a foreign company, issued by the Registrar, must appear in a legible form on all business letters ..." (a duty not met)

@ref s 375(3) (src:24593-24596)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 375 act`
`s 375(3) the foreign company must cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form on its business letters and other documents` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 375(3) cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 375(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the unique entity number did not appear in a legible form" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (4) a foreign company incorporated before 3 January 2016 "need only comply with subsection (3) after the expiration of 12 months after that date".
-- The 12 months are counted P4 (sg-periods.l4): they expire on 3 January 2017; compliance is due from the day after.
-- src:24600 | (4) Despite subsection (3), a foreign company incorporated before
-- src:24601 | 3 January 2016 need only comply with subsection (3) after the
-- src:24602 | expiration of 12 months after that date.
@ref s 375(4) (src:24600-24602)
GIVEN `the foreign company was incorporated before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company was incorporated before 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a foreign company incorporated before 3 January 2016" names the companies the relief reaches, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `the day asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day 3 January 2016` 12 Months
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need only comply with subsection (3) after the expiration of 12 months after that date"

§ `Section 376: service of a document on a foreign company`

-- src:24606 | Service of document
-- src:24608 | 376. Any document required to be served on a foreign company is
-- src:24609 | sufficiently served —
-- src:24611 | (a) if addressed to the foreign company and left at or sent by
-- src:24612 | post to its registered office in Singapore;
-- src:24614 | (b) if addressed to an authorised representative of the company
-- src:24615 | and left at or sent by post to his or her residential address or
-- src:24616 | contact address; or
-- src:24620 | (c) in the case of a foreign company which has ceased to
-- src:24621 | maintain a place of business in Singapore, if addressed to
-- src:24622 | the foreign company and left at or sent by post to its
-- src:24623 | registered office in the place of its incorporation.
@ref s 376 (src:24606-24623)
GIVEN `the document is required to be served on the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is addressed to the foreign company and left at, or sent by post to, its registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is addressed to an authorised representative of the company and left at, or sent by post to, his or her residential address or contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has ceased to maintain a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is addressed to the foreign company and left at, or sent by post to, its registered office in the place of its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is required to be served on the foreign company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any document required to be served on a foreign company" names the documents it reaches
    ELSE (IF    `the document is addressed to the foreign company and left at, or sent by post to, its registered office in Singapore`
             OR `the document is addressed to an authorised representative of the company and left at, or sent by post to, his or her residential address or contact address`
             OR (`the foreign company has ceased to maintain a place of business in Singapore` AND `the document is addressed to the foreign company and left at, or sent by post to, its registered office in the place of its incorporation`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficiently served — (a) if addressed to the foreign company and left at or sent by post to its registered office in Singapore; (b) if addressed to an authorised representative ...; or (c) in the case of a foreign company which has ceased to maintain a place of business in Singapore, if addressed to the foreign company and left at or sent by post to its registered office in the place of its incorporation" (a condition the text introduces with "if": marginal reading (a); the other reading is NOTHING, since other ways of serving are not excluded)
